{"key": "[\"The town is named for Mamalla, the Pallava king who took the Chalukya capital, Vatapi, in 642. By the sea, granite becomes shrines, chariots of single rock, and a vast relief read as Arjuna's penance, or the Ganga's descent. From this port Pallava letters sail east, to become Khmer, Thai and Javanese script.\", \"sarvam:varun_en_suspense@en-IN\", \"+6%\", \"+0Hz\", {}, \"fx5\"]", "mp3": "/Users/saidevdhal/Desktop/Codes/indianepics/public/audio/en/mamallapuram.mp3", "duration": 23.051708, "words": [{"t": 0.0, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "The"}, {"t": 0.4349378867924529, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "town"}, {"t": 0.8698757735849058, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "is"}, {"t": 1.3048136603773586, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "named"}, {"t": 1.7397515471698115, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "for"}, {"t": 2.174689433962264, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "Mamalla,"}, {"t": 2.609627320754717, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "the"}, {"t": 3.04456520754717, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "Pallava"}, {"t": 3.479503094339623, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "king"}, {"t": 3.914440981132076, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "who"}, {"t": 4.349378867924528, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "took"}, {"t": 4.784316754716982, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "the"}, {"t": 5.219254641509434, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "Chalukya"}, {"t": 5.654192528301888, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "capital,"}, {"t": 6.08913041509434, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "Vatapi,"}, {"t": 6.5240683018867935, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "in"}, {"t": 6.959006188679246, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "642."}, {"t": 7.3939440754716985, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "By"}, {"t": 7.828881962264152, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "the"}, {"t": 8.263819849056604, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "sea,"}, {"t": 8.698757735849057, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "granite"}, {"t": 9.133695622641511, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "becomes"}, {"t": 9.568633509433964, "d": 0.4349378867924529, "w": "shrines,"}, {"t": 